<title>LITHUANIA: GOV'T SAYS WILL PAY GAZPROM DEBT IN APRIL.</title>
<headline>GOV'T SAYS WILL PAY GAZPROM DEBT IN APRIL.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Lithuanian government said on Thursday that it will pay all of the 1994-1996 debts owed to Russian gas supplier Gazprom in April.</p>
<p>The government said in a statement that the country still owes Gazprom around 50 million litas.</p>
<p>It said that 30 million litas of the debt would be paid by Lithuania Energy and Lithuanian Gas and the remaining 20 million litas will be paid from the state budget.</p>
<p>--Vilnius newsroom, +370 2 22 35 17</p>
</text>
